### A seventh-order dispersive equation whose seventh-order term is the
### whole spatial operator.
###
###   u_t + u_7x = 0   on  x in [-1.95, 1.95],  t in [0, 0.25]
###   u* = cosh(mu (x - mu^6 t)),  mu = 1.3,  mu^6 = 4.827
###
### The solution is deliberately not sinusoidal.  In the companion case
### pinn_disp7 the exact solution is a sine, which gives the SIN
### activation a structural advantage: its own functional form is the
### answer.  A hyperbolic cosine removes that, and if anything favours
### tanh, which is built from the same exponentials.
###
### This is the case bench/zk7 is not.  There the coefficient relations
### of the soliton family fix the balance between the terms, and the
### seventh-order term sits at a few per cent of the leading one however
### k is chosen, so the equation is solved without the seventh derivative
### ever being represented well.
###
### Here the whole spatial operator IS the seventh derivative, so the
### residual weights it alone rather than burying it under a leading
### term.  Two limits should be stated.  A seventh-order spatial operator
### needs more boundary traces than the one Dirichlet value per wall
### supplied here, so this is a manufactured collocation test, not a
### well-posed initial-boundary-value problem.  And the seventh
### derivative is not pinned individually even so: an error e that itself
### satisfies e_t + e_7x = 0 leaves the residual untouched, so the time
### derivative and the seventh derivative can be wrong together.  What
### the case does compare is how well each activation lets the network
### carry a solution whose residual is dominated by one high order.
###
### The initial condition and the two spatial boundaries are supplied as
### an ordinary DATA term; the residual determines the rest.
Init_w       Glorot_norm
Rand_seed    20260804 /
Restart      0 /
Output_deriv 0 /

Nlayer       4 / L
2 / ndim(1) = D0 = (x, t)
30 /
30 /
1 / ndim(L)

Loss_term  DATA         150  data.dat    1.d0  / initial condition and walls
Loss_term  COLLOCATION  600  colloc.dat  1.d-3 / interior

Residual 2 /
LIN   1.d0    0 1 /   u_t
LIN   1.d0    7 0 /   u_7x
Exact_solution 1 /

Hod_K      7 /
1.d0
0.d0
0.d0
0.d0
0.d0
0.d0
0.d0
0.d0
Hod_dense  0 /   the closure of the residual indices

Hod_check  1 /
Num_validation 60 /
Validation_cyc 500 /
P_max          2000 /
Epoch      20000 /
Activation TANH /
Conv       1.d-14 /
Num_batch  40 /
Checkpoint_cyc 100000 /
GD_method  Adam
GD_param   0.002d0 0.9d0 0.999d0 1.d-8 0.d0 /
